00:41:25,270 --> 00:41:27,270
And then for impact is all about the use case.

377
00:41:27,270 --> 00:41:33,910
Am I building a PC or a spike or is this like a super critical business flow that I'm working on?

378
00:41:33,910 --> 00:41:38,069
And then detectability is all about how easy will it be for me to see that it did something wrong.

379
00:41:38,069 --> 00:41:41,109
So what are my feedback loops? What do I have in place?

380
00:41:41,109 --> 00:41:45,430
And then when I look at all of those things, then I decide how much do I let it go unsupervised?

381
00:41:45,430 --> 00:41:47,510
How much review do I want to do?

382
00:41:47,510 --> 00:41:53,030
Do I want to look at every single line of code or just like a highle thing just check the sensors and I'm done.

383
00:41:53,030 --> 00:42:02,470
And yeah to go back to the probability right probability then is also a lot about how much confidence I have in my guides and sensors how much visibility do I have into the things that

